# MT6755 matrix keypad.
#
# Physically populated keys: Volume Up, Volume Down, Power. The driver also
# advertises KEY_HOME (102) and KEY_RESTART (408) because they exist in the
# MT6755 reference matrix, but neither is wired to a switch on this chassis.
# Both are deliberately left undeclared: an undeclared scan code resolves to
# AKEYCODE_UNKNOWN and InputReader drops it. Without this file the device falls
# back to Generic.kl, which maps 102 to MOVE_HOME -- a phantom matrix scan would
# then inject a text-cursor key into whatever has focus.
#
# WAKE on the volume keys is what LineageOS's "Volume buttons wake device"
# option needs: PhoneWindowManager derives isWakeKey from FLAG_WAKE and then
# gates it on LineageSettings.System.VOLUME_WAKE_SCREEN in isWakeKeyEnabled()
# and isWakeKeyWhenScreenOff(). With the setting off the flag has no effect, so
# declaring WAKE here does not cause spurious wakes.
#
# WAKE on POWER is the AOSP convention. PhoneWindowManager clears isWakeKey for
# KEYCODE_POWER and wakes through interceptPowerKeyDown() instead, so the flag
# is inert there; it is stated for consistency with every AOSP keylayout.

key 114   VOLUME_DOWN   WAKE
key 115   VOLUME_UP     WAKE
key 116   POWER         WAKE
